# Cloudflare Pages response headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/).
# Security headers for every response.
#
# The CSP is Report-Only first: on a preview deploy, go through the first screen,
# connect (camera), relays, rates, lock (passkey), PIN and lightning address lookup on
# a phone and read the console for violations. With none, rename
# the header to Content-Security-Policy. scripts/check-csp.ts reads this file.
#
# connect-src is https: wss: because users pick their own relays and their own Lightning
# address domains (and the callback hosts those name); it stops injected scripts, not code
# that is already running. src/lib/lnurl's host rule keeps lookups off private hosts.
# img-src has no https: because remote profile pictures are not drawn.
# worker-src blob: is the QR scanner's worker; style-src 'unsafe-inline' is React's
# inline styles. Each header appears once: Pages joins repeated headers with commas.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), bluetooth=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https: wss:; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/manifest.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json
